  "summary": "The San Francisco Human Rights Commission found that SFPD did not violate the city's sanctuary law when out-of-state and federal agencies accessed its Flock license plate reader data, because a Flock 'Nationwide Lookup' setting was enabled without SFPD's knowledge. The report nonetheless issued five recommendations to tighten oversight, including shortening retention to 30 days, requiring documented search justifications, and considering alternate vendors; advocates called for SFPD to end its Flock contract.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "While the evidence does not support a finding against SFPD \u2026 HRC's investigation shows that SFPD's contractor allowed city resources to be utilized to arguably assist in enforcement of federal immigration law",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "the San Francisco Standard had earlier reported 1.6 million such illegal searches between 2024 and 2025",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "The police should wipe license plate data after 30 days",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "She said San Francisco should not renew its Flock contract.",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    }
